05445132327</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B4"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Enns</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Packmann</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The adolescent with an inborn error of metabolism: medical issues and transition to adulthood</article-title><source>Adolesc Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>329</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11986039</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mudd</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Levy</surname><given-names>HL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kraus</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Scriver CR, Beaudet AL, Sly WS, Valle D</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Disorders of transulfuration</article-title><source>The Metabolic and Molecular Basis of Inherited Disease</source><year>2001</year><volume>2</volume><edition>8</edition><publisher-name>New York: McGraw-Hill</publisher-name><fpage>2007</fpage><lpage>2056</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shih</surname><given-names>VE</given-names></name><name><surname>Fringer</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mandell</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Kraus</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Berry</surname><given-names>GT</given-names></name><name><surname>Heidenrich</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Korson</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Levy</surname><given-names>HL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramesh</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>missense mutation (I278T) in the cystathionine beta-synthase gene prevalent in pyridoxine-responsive homocystinuria and associated with mild clinical phenotype</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>1995</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>34</fpage><lpage>39</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7611293</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>